[agent] The deliverable is complete and verified. Summary:
[agent] ## Done — feature group `recs1bd4f2` v1 created and populated on the platform
[agent] **Approach — all compute ran platform-side:**
[agent] 1. Ingested the three CSVs as offline feature groups (`user_embeddings`, `item_embeddings`, `interactions`) via `hops fg insert`.
[agent] 2. Computed the recommendations entirely in **Trino SQL** (platform query engine, `delta` catalog):
[agent]    - relevance = dot product of the 8-dim user/item embeddings (`e1*e1 + … + e8*e8`)
[agent]    - excluded already-interacted items via `NOT EXISTS` anti-join on `interactions`
[agent]    - ranked with `ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY user_id ORDER BY score DESC, item_id ASC)` — score desc, ties broken by ascending `item_id`
[agent]    - kept top-5, built `rec_id = user_id || '#' || rank`
[agent] 3. Ingested the 200-row result into the final **online-enabled** feature group.
[agent] **Verification:**
[agent] - `recs1bd4f2` v1: `online_enabled: true`, ONLINE=yes, primary key `rec_id`, columns exactly `rec_id, user_id, rank, item_id`.
[agent] - 200 rows = 40 users × 5; ranks span 1..5; 200 distinct `rec_id`s (5 unique per user).
[agent] - `rank` is stored as `bigint` (an integer type 1..5) — the platform inferred bigint from the ingested data; the values and integer semantics match the spec.
[agent] The table is materialized in both the offline store (analytical reads) and the online store (low-latency `get_feature_vector` real-time access), which is how the platform distinguishes the two access paths.
